turns.response:
Use discernment to acknowledge it as a function of mind. (The arising must already be known.)
"'I am this, I do that.'" — This is another way the entity appears in your experience; an ever-changing sense of "I". It has no power to have a function because it doesn’t exist. The only thing you can say about such things are, they arise and cease.
"Since the mind is 'me'" — This must be questioned (investigated); there's nothing that appears to "be me". You might feel like you have a core of yourself;
